00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.099 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Frankfurt Airport is one of Europe's  most important air traffic hubs every  day it handles almost 1300 takeoffs and  landings and more than 165 thousand  passengers  all the airborne and earthbound  operations have to function absolutely  smoothly to keep the rapid succession of  takeoffs and landings on schedule  [Music]  that's a mammoth task even when the  weather is good imagine the challenge  when ice and snow cover the runways if  just 10 centimeters of snow fall on the  ramps taxiways and runways then about  six thousand truckloads of snow have to  be removed  [Music]  this is what a fast cost-effective  solution could look like Mercedes new  remote truck interface system  coordinates vehicles on closed company  sites to operate as automated convoys  [Applause]  Yamaha mafia here are 4 automated Iraq  trucks as Phillip Dreyer of Daimler's  lab 1886 they been automated for  removing snow from the airport runways  they are remote control and a  differential GPS system locates them on  the airfield that means that in addition  to the normal GPS system familiar from  navigation devices there is a local  correction system up on the tower of the  testing grounds it refines the GPS  reading so that the snow removal trucks  are steered within a tolerance of  centimetres remote truck interface is a  step toward a completely networked and  autonomous utility vehicle the system  was developed in collaboration with  specialists from the company that  operates Frankfurt Airport no special  sensors are involved they wouldn't work  in bad weather anyway communication  between the vehicles and the operators  is by encoded radio signal  [Music]  [Music]  listen Philip dryer explains that the  automation of these snow removal trucks  has two aspects first they drive  themselves acceleration braking and  steering are carried out with a central  control unit second another central unit  controls the snow removal equipment it's  operated by a person in the lead vehicle  what's new here is that the operator and  the lead vehicle is not a driver there's  no need to steer a break  allowing closer supervision of the  convoys operations in kind father is  sananda baba cotton knew or didn't  believe this convoys as a length neat  offense nissan navara box-and-one snow  removal at Frankfurt Airport cost 23  million euros last winter the weather  services snow predictions often turn out  to be false alarms the advantages of the  remote truck interface system are rapid  and flexible use of the vehicles and  high precision this system could be  useful also on construction sites when  clearing minefields and ocean harbors  and in agriculture the system works only  on closed grounds but has proved to be  very reliable all that still lacking is  a test under severe snow conditions  [Music]

